    "https://tulane-ibqejb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/1499": {
      "title": "Surgical Pathologist",
      "description": "The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine at Tulane University School of Medicine is seeking applications for a position in anatomic pathology. Candidates should have a medical degree (MD or MD/PhD, or the equivalent) be board-certified/eligible in AP, or AP/CP with proper subspecialty fellowship training, preferably in GU, Gyn/breast, pulmonary or head-and-neck pathology. The candidate should be eligible for a Louisiana Medical License. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with experience.\nDuties will include sign-out of general surgical pathology cases, and teaching for medical students, residents, and fellows. Research activities will include any scholastic activities that pertain to the applicant’s clinical and/or academic interests. Service responsibilities will include serving on Departmental and/or University committees when needed.\n",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://tulane-ibqejb.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/1457": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer",
      "description": "Position Description:\n\nThe Historic Preservation Program at Tulane University invites applications for an Adjunct Lecturer to teach conservation science and conservation technology courses. The instructor will teach 9–12 credits over the academic year, with courses focused on the material science, analysis, documentation, and hands-on treatment of historic building materials.\nThis position is intended for a practitioner-scholar with demonstrated expertise in architectural conservation, historic building materials, preservation treatments, and field- or lab-based instruction. The successful candidate will be able to teach students how to understand historic buildings as material systems, diagnose deterioration, communicate conservation needs, and apply preservation best practices through demonstrations, mock-ups, documentation, and specifications.\n",
      "department": null
    },
